{"id": "EUVD-2026-75632", "enisaUuid": "fcd3e864-4663-3aa6-9a99-f9ee83a28ba2", "description": "passport-saml-encrypted through 0.1.13 contains an XML signature wrapping vulnerability where signature verification and assertion extraction use independent XPath lookups with no cross-validation. Attackers holding any validly signed SAML message can prepend a forged unsigned assertion that gets accepted as the verified identity while the genuine signature validates against the original assertion.", "datePublished": "2026-09-10T17:39:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-10T17:53:56", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/krakenjs/passport-saml-encrypted/issues/30", "https://github.com/krakenjs/passport-saml-encrypted/blob/v0.1.13/lib/saml.js#L256", "https://github.com/krakenjs/passport-saml-encrypted/blob/v0.1.13/lib/saml.js#L328", "https://github.com/krakenjs/passport-saml-encrypted", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/passport-saml-encrypted-through-0.1.13-xml-signature-wrapping-via-assertion-prepending"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89043", "GHSA-8vr8-32m4-xw8q"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "64079d66-77e8-3da3-8a75-b5056f2a367c", "product": {"name": "passport-saml-encrypted", "vendor": {"name": "krakenjs"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.1.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "22ab3707-a2d7-358e-941e-389a32d5fc99", "vendor": {"name": "krakenjs"}}], "isExploited": false}